This repository began as a clone of that repository and retains its full git
history, so every upstream commit remains attributable. The MIT licence and the
original copyright notice are reproduced below, as that licence requires.

What is inherited from upstream:

  - The repository history and the MIT licence.
  - `src/index.js`, the single-site stdio MCP server. It is retained verbatim
    apart from a provenance header, so existing stdio users keep working.

What is new in this repository (GPL-3.0-only):

  - The portable core, the local stdio edition, and the Cloudflare Workers
    deployment: an authorization server Worker, an MCP resource server Worker,
    D1 schema, and OAuth 2.1 wiring.
  - The expanded tool catalogue, the proposal/approval workflow, capability
    detection, content intelligence, and the SSRF policy.
  - The entire test suite, the documentation, and the deployment configuration.

None of the upstream code is presented as independently authored. See
`docs/UPSTREAM_COMPARISON.md` for a file-by-file account.

